The random program works now.

here's how to get random image samples:

% random -s seed -n #pixels -r sline,lline,ssamp,lsamp | sort -n > pts

the file pts will contain random line and sample numbers.

[note that you must specify a seed each time you run this.
if you don't give a seed, it will always print the same
random numbers.]

now you can use primg to get the pixel values.

for S readable image random samples:

% foreach i (slope elev radiation ...)
> primg -i $i -p pts > $i.S
> end
%

or if you want ipw readable random sample images:

% mkhdr -l nlines -s nsamps > hdr

% foreach i (slope elev radiation ...)
> cp hdr $i.ipw
> primg -i $i -c pts >> $i.ipw
> end

%

let me know if you have any questions or problems.

